sarge ’pi nopajāyante
pralaye na vyathanti ca\"}]},{\"section\":\"synonyms\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.synonyms\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"books.Synonyms\",\"title\":\"synonyms\",\"id\":3833,\"bb\":3375,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/2/b3375/\",\"shadow_value\":\"idam – this; jñānam – knowledge; upāśritya – taking shelter of; mama – My; sādharmyam – same nature; āgatāḥ – having attained; sarge api – even in the creation; na – never; upajāyante – are born; pralaye – in the annihilation; na – nor; vyathanti – are disturbed; ca – also.\",\"word_for_word_value\":[{\"word\":\"idam\",\"translation\":\"this\"},{\"word\":\"jñānam\",\"translation\":\"knowledge\"},{\"word\":\"upāśritya\",\"translation\":\"taking shelter of\"},{\"word\":\"mama\",\"translation\":\"My\"},{\"word\":\"sādharmyam\",\"translation\":\"same nature\"},{\"word\":\"āgatāḥ\",\"translation\":\"having attained\"},{\"word\":\"sarge api\",\"translation\":\"even in the creation\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"never\"},{\"word\":\"upajāyante\",\"translation\":\"are born\"},{\"word\":\"pralaye\",\"translation\":\"in the annihilation\"},{\"word\":\"na\",\"translation\":\"nor\"},{\"word\":\"vyathanti\",\"translation\":\"are disturbed\"},{\"word\":\"ca\",\"translation\":\"also\"}]}]},{\"section\":\"translation\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.translation\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"translation\",\"id\":3834,\"bb\":3376,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/2/b3376/\",\"body_value\":\"By becoming fixed in this knowledge, one can attain to the transcendental nature like My own. Thus established, one is not born at the time of creation or disturbed at the time of dissolution.\"}]},{\"section\":\"purport\",\"section_title\":\"Books.Verse.purport\",\"children\":[{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3835,\"bb\":3377,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/2/b3377/\",\"body_value\":\"After acquiring perfect transcendental knowledge, one acquires qualitative equality with the Supreme Personality of Godhead, becoming free from the repetition of birth and death. One does not, however, lose his identity as an individual soul. It is understood from Vedic literature that the liberated souls who have reached the transcendental planets of the spiritual sky always look to the lotus feet of the Supreme Lord, being engaged in His transcendental loving service. So, even after liberation, the devotees do not lose their individual identities.\"},{\"type\":\"content.Record\",\"title\":\"paragraph\",\"id\":3836,\"bb\":3378,\"url_path\":\"/en/library/bg/14/2/b3378/\",\"body_value\":\"$25\"}]}],\"short_title\":\"Bg. 14.2\",\"medium_title\":\"Bhagavad-gītā As It Is 14.2\"},\"locale\":\"en\",\"activeView\":\"$6:props:activeView\"}]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\"]}]\n"])self.__next_f.push([1,"2a:I[83068,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n30:I[78455,[\"/_next/static/chunks/130enlymdm.jk.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0b6f_zxj9ay~6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/143cg6c13uly6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/07vk.k35-e~ti.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0j6k6n9cniknh.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0.zxv9arc6a56.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00-zmo-3n1bt8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0p4z5tusn0jt6.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/01mcazkjru_is.js\"],\"default\"]\n26:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-4 w-full max-w-screen-xl mx-auto md:px-8 mb-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"nav\",null,{\"aria-label\":\"Breadcrumb\",\"className\":\"breadcrumb mb-8 text-base\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"/en/library/\",{\"className\":\"inline\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L20\",null,{\"href\":\"/en/library/\",\"className\":\"text-